# layer_norm smoke — PR gate: the row shape and the optional-parameter families
#
# Shape column = the case's view: MxNxK with
#   M = rows, N = norm_size, K = 1
# and the params column carries the normalization in the fixed key order
#   rows,ns[,e][,sc][,sh]
# (see tests/inputs/README.md). The two columns must agree; a mismatch is a
# parse error. e is eps scaled by 1e9 (e0 = 0, e10000 = 1e-5), sc selects
# use_scale and sh selects use_shift (1 = read the STAT_SCALE / STAT_SHIFT
# vector, 0 = the constant 1 / 0).
#
# f32 is bit-exact against the scalar golden; f16/bf16 compare at the dtype
# trait tolerance (exact up-conversion, fp32 accumulation).
